# `Tcaches`'s byte offsets and layout, which the build checks with `fits`.
T_TABLE	core library	Kani	discharged (const assert: `axiom_tcaches_layout` in src/heap/tcaches.rs)	contract 2097268554, body none
T_LOCK	core library	Kani	discharged (const assert: `axiom_tcaches_layout` in src/heap/tcaches.rs)	contract 2489631139, body none
T_INV	core library	Kani	discharged (const assert: `axiom_tcaches_layout` in src/heap/tcaches.rs)	contract 1448314863, body none
axiom_tcaches_layout	core library	Kani	discharged (const assert: `axiom_tcaches_layout` in src/heap/tcaches.rs)	contract 623019862, body none
# Joining typed field permissions into the struct's: no vstd counterpart.
# The harness runs `Tcaches::init`, the one call, which
# `crate::tests::assembled_writes_only_at_checked_sites` pins, and checks
# that its writes leave every field byte of the `Tcaches` as the axiom's
# `ensures` state.
axiom_tcaches_assemble	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: heap::tcaches::kani_assemble::init_writes_every_field; not checked: the join itself, that the field permissions and `pad` may be exchanged for one `PointsTo<Tcaches>` at `p`, with its provenance, a premise of Verus's own model that no tool checks; the ghost identities the `ensures` carries over, each table entry's atomic identity (`vspec::entry::entry_id`, which the `inv`'s key records) and the lock's cell identity, which Kani does not observe; and the ghost fields (`inv`, the lock's rank and initial value), which have no bytes)	contract 2226354314, body none
# The C caller uses an explicit cache on one thread at a time: each
# `MALLOCX_TCACHE` call and `tcache.flush` makes one token, before any
# reference `Tcaches::get` lends.
axiom_heap_use	C-program contract	none (assumption)
# The same contract, about the table's registry: when `Tcaches::get`
# loads a non-null entry, or `Tcaches::destroy` swaps one out, the
# permission to its heap is in the registry, because no other caller
# holds it out (one thread at a time, each `get` followed by `put_back`,
# pinned by `every_get_puts_back`). Called only in `get` and `destroy`
# (pinned by `entry_heap_axiom_only_in_get_and_destroy`). It states
# nothing of the heap: the registry's invariant does.
axiom_entry_heap	C-program contract	none (assumption)
